Two-sided stencil drew no quads (2026-11-23, David Sharp's d3gltest)

- swrast_setup/ss_tritmp.h: two-sided stencil makes swrast_setup take its
  unfilled-polygon path, to know each triangle's facing. There a quad was
  drawn only if the vertex buffer had edge flags, which tnl gives only
  for GL_LINE/GL_POINT polygon modes, so with both modes GL_FILL every
  quad (glBegin(GL_QUADS)) was dropped: the shadow volume itself, and
  every quad after it until the triangle functions were chosen again
  (Mesa's own comment there: "this test shouldn't be needed (bug
  12614)"). Without edge flags the quad is now its two triangles.

--- a/src/mesa/swrast_setup/ss_tritmp.h
+++ b/src/mesa/swrast_setup/ss_tritmp.h
@@ -227,6 +227,14 @@
          VB->EdgeFlag[v3] = 0;
          TAG(triangle)( ctx, v1, v2, v3 );
          VB->EdgeFlag[v3] = ef3;
+      } else {
+         /* riscos-mesa: no edge flags (both modes GL_FILL: this path is
+          * taken for two-sided stencil, which needs each triangle's
+          * facing). The quad was dropped, and so was every quad after it
+          * until the triangle functions were chosen again (David Sharp,
+          * d3gltest: two-sided stencil shadow volumes in software). */
+         TAG(triangle)( ctx, v0, v1, v3 );
+         TAG(triangle)( ctx, v1, v2, v3 );
       }
    } else {
       TAG(triangle)( ctx, v0, v1, v3 );
